# Architecture

Hexagonal, with the dependency rule **enforced by crate boundaries** (the compiler rejects an inward
layer importing an outward one). Decisions and history: `docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`.

```
crates/domain          pure model: sessions, attention, events. serde only — no IO, time, tokio, tauri
crates/application     use cases (WarRoomService), ports (traits), read model (view.rs → TS), locale.rs
crates/infrastructure  adapters: claude/ (provider, transcripts, installer, pricing, skills), ingress,
                       sqlite, git, system, desktop/ (KWin, tmux, Warp), pty, launch
crates/wire            socket contract bridge ↔ app (serde only)
crates/i18n            translation lookup over locales/<lang>.json (serde_json only); used by every
                       crate that shows text, the front reads the same catalogs
crates/hook-bridge     `warroom-hook`, the binary Claude runs on every hook
src-tauri              composition root + driving adapters (commands) + tray/notifications
src/                   React: domain · application · infrastructure · ui (same rule inside)
```

`domain ← application ← infrastructure ← src-tauri`. The front mirrors it: `ui → application →
domain`; `infrastructure/` implements the ports in `application/ports.ts`.

## Where does X go?

| X | Place |
|---|---|
| A rule about session state (what an event does) | `crates/domain/src/session.rs` (+ test in `room.rs`) |
| Something the core needs from the outside world | a port in `crates/application/src/ports.rs`, its adapter in `crates/infrastructure`, wired in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs` **and** the e2e `Room::start` |
| What the UI receives | `crates/application/src/view.rs` (TS types regenerate from it) |
| Derived data that must not be persisted (transcript facts, pending approvals, stall notices) | fields of `WarRoomService`, never the domain |
| Agent-specific knowledge (hook dialect, transcript shape, prices, config paths) | `crates/infrastructure/src/<agent>/` (`claude/`, `codex/`) — the domain must not know any agent |
| Something several agents share (hook protocol, installer, JSONL reading, skill folders, tool labels) | `hooks.rs`, `hook_installer.rs`, `jsonl.rs`, `skills.rs`, `tools.rs` in `crates/infrastructure/src/` |
| User-visible text | a key in every `locales/*.json`, exposed by the crate's `locale.rs` / `src/domain/copy.ts` (`i18n.mdc`) |
| A Tauri command or event | `src-tauri/src/commands.rs` / `adapters.rs`, mirrored in `src/infrastructure/tauriGateway.ts` |

## Ports (crates/application/src/ports.rs)

AgentProvider · RepoResolver · EventStore · Clock · ProcessProbe · Notifier · ViewPublisher ·
TranscriptReader · WindowNavigator · AgentLauncher · SessionInput · SkillCatalog · GitHistory ·
ApprovalResponder · IntegrationInstaller. All bundled in `service::Ports`; what is specific to one
agent (provider, transcripts, skills) comes as an `AgentPorts` per agent in `Ports.agents`, and the
service picks it by the session's `ProviderKind`. A new port means: trait + fake in `service.rs` tests
+ real adapter + wiring in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs` + the e2e harness (`tests/e2e/mod.rs`).

## Service rules (crates/application/src/service.rs)

- Every state change is a `SessionEvent` through `commit()`: apply → persist → refresh transcript →
  publish → notify. User intents (seen, archive, mute) are events too.
- Lock order: `room` → `summaries` → `approvals` → `stalled`. Don't call slow ports while holding
  `room` (only pure projections).
- Transcript reads happen off the startup path (`refresh_all_summaries` in a thread) and on each
  agent event / tick for live sessions (background completion may arrive after the main turn ends).
- `view::effective_attention` overlays transcript-confirmed background commands and automatic permission
  review on domain attention.
  Views, tray aggregates, completion notices and acknowledgements share this rule; a tick notifies
  when the final pending command completes. Transcript-derived command counts are never persisted.

## Adding a new agent provider (Codex, Gemini, opencode…)

The domain is provider-agnostic. Skill `add-provider` has the checklist.
